  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development to which this permission relates must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of the decision notice. \rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be implemented and maintained in accordance with the following approved plans and documents:\r\rLocation and Block Plan - E 00\rProposed Location and Block Plan - P 00\rProposed Site Plan - P 01\rProposed Floor and Roof Plan - P 02\rProposed Front and Side Elevation Plan - P 03\rProposed Rear and Side Elevation Plan - P 04\rProposed Section AA Plan - P 05\rProposed Cycle Storage Plan - P 06\rProposed Refuse Storage Plan - P 07\rHighways Proforma\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r\r",
    "The use of the property as a House in Multiple Occupation hereby approved shall be occupied by a maximum of 7 people at any one time and shall not be subdivided or occupied as self-contained units.\r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "No independent cooking or laundry facilities shall be installed in any of the respective bedrooms and the communal kitchen shall be retained in perpetuity.\r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "Prior to occupation, the cycle parking facilities as shown on the approved drawings shall be implemented in full and shall thereafter be retained.\r\rReason: To ensure the provision of secure and adequate cycle parking and promote sustainable mode of transport.\r",
    "Prior to occupation, the refuse and recycling storage areas as shown on the approved drawings shall be implemented in full and shall thereafter be retained and maintained.\r\rReason: To ensure adequate and secure refuse and recycling provision in the interests of amenity.\r"
  ],
